From 5fdeb042a18160a8bd67292fc27121add2573f44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:45:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the picture-in-picture streams of a Blu-ray are
 never the ones the player opens by itself

A clip of a Blu-ray can carry a picture-in-picture video (PIDs 0x1B00 to
0x1B1F) and a secondary audio stream (0x1A00 to 0x1A1F) beside the film,
which a player shows over it when the disc's menus ask for it; Kodi has
neither the picture-in-picture nor the mixer. With the disc's menus the
player opened the first video stream whose packet came first, which can be
the picture-in-picture one; for a playlist played directly it opened the
first video stream of the demuxer and the best-ranked audio stream, which
can be either of them.

Now IsBetterStream() never takes a picture-in-picture video of a Blu-ray
for the film, and OpenDefaultStreams() ranks both kinds after the other
streams of their type, unless the user chose one for this file. They stay
among the streams that can be chosen, and the demuxer says in the log which
ones they are (BluraySecondaryStreams.h).

The idea is SamuriHL's (CoreELEC, "a bluray secondary audio track is never
the soundtrack", by Alex Scotti) and pannal's (CoreELEC, the picture-in-
picture video of "30 Minutes or Less"), who leave them out of the demuxer;
here they are kept, ranked last.
